# Intelligent Browser-Based Software Failure Forensics Platform

A full-stack observability platform designed to capture, store, and analyze browser-side telemetry for forensic debugging of silent, delayed, and non-reproducible software failures.

---

## Overview

The system acts as a **"Black Box Recorder for Web Applications"** — capturing rich structured telemetry from monitored web apps via a Chrome Extension, compressing and uploading it to a backend pipeline, and exposing it through role-based dashboards for forensic investigation.

```mermaid
flowchart LR
    A[Browser Extension] -->|NDJSON+ZSTD| B[Ingestion API]
    B --> C[Processing Pipeline]
    C --> D[(ClickHouse)]
    C --> E[(S3/R2)]
    C --> F[(Vector Store)]
    D --> G[Dashboard / WebSocket]
    G --> H[Developer UI]
    G --> I[Creator / Admin UI]
```

---

## Platform Components

| Layer | Technology | Purpose |
|-------|-----------|---------|
| Browser Extension | Chrome MV3, JS | Telemetry capture + local buffering |
| Frontend Dashboard | Next.js 14, TailwindCSS | Role-based UI for Admin + Developer |
| API Gateway | Node.js + Fastify | Auth, rate limiting, tenant isolation |
| Ingestion Service | Node.js / Go | Receive + decompress + validate chunks |
| Processing Pipeline | Node.js workers / BullMQ | Normalize, dedupe, fingerprint, enrich |
| Timeline Engine | Node.js | Reconstruct session timelines |
| Real-time Streaming | WebSocket / SSE | Live telemetry push to dashboards |
| Hot Storage | ClickHouse | Fast indexed telemetry queries |
| Warm Storage | Cloudflare R2 / S3 | Compressed ZSTD archive (6 months) |
| Vector Store (opt.) | Qdrant / Weaviate | AI semantic search |

