### Phase 3 — Dashboard Frontend (Next.js 14)

**Goal:** Role-based web UI for Admin workspace management and Developer forensic investigation.

#### Creator / Admin Views

| View | Features |
|------|----------|
| Workspace Manager | Create workspaces, register websites, generate extension configs |
| User Management | Invite developers, assign roles, revoke access |
| Analytics Overview | Error trends, top failing APIs, affected users, usage metrics |
| Billing & Settings | Retention config, notification preferences |

#### Developer Views

| View | Features |
|------|----------|
| Live Monitoring Dashboard | Real-time event stream, API failures, performance alerts, active sessions |
| Session Timeline Explorer | Search by user + timestamp, full event timeline visualization, console + network view |
| Incident Investigator | Root cause hypotheses, correlated events, workflow integrity report |
| Bug Tracker Integration | Create/link Jira/Linear issues, auto-attach telemetry snapshot |

#### Key UI Components
- **Timeline Viewer**: Horizontal scrollable event timeline with category swimlanes
- **Event Inspector**: Drill-down panel showing full event payload, stack trace, network response
- **Anomaly Heatmap**: Calendar view of incident density
- **Session Replay** (optional): DOM snapshot-based replay using `rrweb`

---

### Phase 4 — Authentication & Multi-Tenancy

**Goal:** Secure, isolated access for all roles.

#### Creator / Admin Auth
- Email/password + 2FA (TOTP)
- JWT access tokens, refresh token rotation
- Workspace-scoped permissions

#### Developer Auth (Passkey Flow)
- Admin generates a scoped passkey per developer
- Passkey grants read-only access to specific workspace telemetry
- Passkeys are time-limited and revocable

#### Tenant Isolation
- All ClickHouse queries include `WHERE workspace_id = ?`
- R2/S3 objects namespaced under `/{workspaceId}/`
- No cross-tenant data leakage possible at query level

