## Open Questions

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Where do you want to start building?**
> Recommended: Start with the **Browser Extension** (Phase 1) — it is the data source for everything else and can be built and tested independently with mock uploads.

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Hosting preference for the backend?**
> Options: Self-hosted Docker Compose (fastest to start), Railway/Render (managed), or full cloud (AWS/GCP/Cloudflare Workers).

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **ZSTD compression in the extension?**
> Requires a WASM build of `zstd`. Alternative: use browser-native `CompressionStream` (gzip/deflate) for MVP, migrate to ZSTD later. Which do you prefer?

> [!NOTE]
> **Session Replay** (DOM snapshot-based using `rrweb`) is a high-value optional feature. Should this be included in MVP scope?

> [!NOTE]
> **AI features** (Phase 6) require vector embeddings and an LLM integration. These are explicitly post-MVP, but should the vector store schema be designed now to support it later?

